0	# InkOS — Sprint 7 Design Spec: Commissions Engine
1	
2	**From:** Vega (Design Agent)
3	**To:** Koda (Feature Builder)
4	**Date:** 2026-04-15
5	**Stack:** Stack A — Next.js 16.2.3, Tailwind 4, shadcn base-nova, dark-first
6	**Sprint:** 7 — Commissions Engine (Week 16–18)
7	
8	---
9	
10	## 0. Pre-Build Rules (carry all 60 from Sprints 1–6 forward, plus these)
11	
12	61. Migration `20260416000004_commissions.sql` must be confirmed applied before any Sprint 7 UI is written. Tables needed: `commission_rules`, `commission_records`, `commission_adjustments`, `commission_disputes`. All 8 RPCs must be present. Dato confirms readiness before Koda writes line 1.
13	
14	62. **`total_cents` is a GENERATED column** — never include in INSERT or UPDATE payloads. Read from Row type only. Koda must add a lint comment at every `commission_records` upsert site: `// total_cents is GENERATED — omit from writes`.
15	
16	63. **Direct INSERT on `commission_records` and `commission_disputes` is blocked by RLS** (`WITH CHECK (false)`). Use only the RPCs: `approve_commissions`, `cancel_commission`, `recalculate_commission`, `raise_commission_dispute`, `resolve_dispute`. Any `.insert()` call on these tables will throw a 403.
17	
18	64. All money values are stored in cents. Display via `formatCurrency(cents)` from `lib/utils.ts`. `tabular-nums` on every money element. No raw dollar signs with string interpolation.
19	
20	65. `get_studio_commission_dashboard` is `STABLE` — cache with `unstable_cache` TTL 60s. `get_artist_commission_summary` is also `STABLE` — cache TTL 30s (used on artist profile Performance tab where data is expected to be more current).
21	
22	66. **Artist-role data isolation** is enforced at the DB layer via RLS. The UI additionally hides approve/cancel/rule-edit actions when `currentMember.role === 'artist'`. Both layers must be present — never rely on UI alone.
23	
24	67. **Commissions feature gate:** `plans.commissions_enabled` boolean. Check via `useFeatureFlag('commissions')`. On Solo tier, `/commissions` renders `<UpgradeGate variant="inline" feature="commissions" />` (see Section 10). Sidebar item is hidden from the nav entirely for Solo tier — use the same `canDo('commissions.view')` permission pattern from Sprint 6.
25	
26	68. `cancel_commission` is owner-only (not admin). Approve is owner/admin. Recalculate is owner/admin. Raise dispute is artist or owner/admin. Resolve dispute is owner/admin. Enforce in UI via `currentMember.role` checks on action buttons.
27	
28	69. When editing an active commission rule, the spec says: set `effective_until = today - 1 day` on the old rule and INSERT a new rule. This happens in a single Server Action. The old rule row is NOT mutated via direct UPDATE — use the `updateCommissionRule` action which handles the date swap atomically.
29	
30	70. The `CommissionPreview` component is reusable across: rule editor drawer, adjustment modal, and booking creation (Sprint 2 `NewBookingDrawer` enhancement). It is a pure calculation component — no data fetching, all inputs are props.
31	
32	---
